<article class="env-corollary" id="070D">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/070D">Corollary <span data-tag="070D">9.7.3.6</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be a regular cardinal and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be $\kappa $-cocomplete $\infty $-categories. Then a functor $T: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is $\kappa $-bilinear if and only if it is bilinear and preserves $\kappa $-small filtered colimits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathbb {K}$ be the collection of all $\kappa $-small filtered $\infty $-categories. It follows from Corollary <a data-tag="06DX" href="/tag/06DX">9.2.2.23</a> that a functor $T$ is $\kappa $-bilinear if and only if it is both bilinear and $\mathbb {K}$-bilinear. The desired result now follows from Proposition <a data-tag="070C" href="/tag/070C">9.7.3.5</a>, since every filtered $\infty $-category is sifted (Example <a data-tag="02QH" href="/tag/02QH">9.7.2.4</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
